  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Linear and quadratic equations, factoring, inequalities and systems — the algebraic backbone of the syllabus.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Solving equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve linear equations by isolating the variable. For quadratics, factor or use \\( x=\\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\). The discriminant \\( b^{2}-4ac \\) reveals how many real roots exist.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Quadratic formula",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Difference of squares",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^{2}-b^{2}=(a-b)(a+b) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Discriminant",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( b^{2}-4ac \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Absolute value",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( |x|=k\\Rightarrow x=\\pm k \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\( x^{2}-5x+6=0 \\). \\( (x-2)(x-3)=0 \\): \\[ x=2\\ \\text{or}\\ x=3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 1.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\( x^{2}+2x-8=0 \\). \\( (x+4)(x-2)=0 \\): \\[ x=-4\\ \\text{or}\\ x=2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "warn",
        "label": {
          "en": "Practice Problem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve \\(2x^2-5x-3=0\\) by factoring, and verify using the quadratic formula. <details><summary>Show solution</summary><div>Factor: \\((2x+1)(x-3)=0\\Rightarrow x=-\\frac{1}{2}\\) or \\(x=3.\\) Verify: \\(\\Delta=25+24=49.\\quad x=\\frac{5\\pm7}{4}\\Rightarrow x=3\\) or \\(x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\) &#x2713;</div></details>",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
